# `&` is only valid as the argument to an inout parameter. A ref binding is not
# a feature (the design-aggregate-ref finding: the compatible constructs are
# in-place inout and yielding subscripts); it would emit a C initializer taken
# from a pointer, which is invalid C.
# expect: is only valid as the argument to an inout parameter
fn main():
    a: [int] = []
    r := &a
    print(str(len(r)))
